                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I want to like this game. A somewhat colorful action-RPG with platforming elements sounds great on paper, and the story has its moments. But the combat, intended to feel like a cool mix between melee and ranged combat a la Devil May Cry, doesn't really flow that well, and mostly devolves to using ranged combat unless you're forced to engage, and several encounters feel either frustrating where one hit means you then get comboed again and again and again because you can't recover fast enough, or tedious, where the enemy isn't really doing anything and you're just mashing the B button to slowly deplete its health. There are neat ideas and puzzles here, but the execution just doesn't carry the weight it needs to. The camera is an issue. Animation priority becomes an issue (I fell off a moving platform because when I hit the switch my character stopped moving with the platform, therefore fell off and I had to do the entire section over again). The cool abilities are completely useless due to casting times when you get swamped by enemies or a boss that just rushes you, meaning all you're doing is dodging and trying to get in a few hits with basic abilities. By the end, I was more happy I got the \"True ending\" as it meant I could in good conscience put the game down rather than feeling like I'd done something.\r\nIt's a shame, but the bad kind of friction really lets this one down.",
